 Client for `inventory-api`. Every function takes a `transport`,
 `async (request) => response`, so callers choose HTTP, IPC or a fake.
 
-- `listItems(transport)` → every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `listItems(transport)` → every item, in server page order (the server
+  orders by `id`). `GET /items` is
+  paginated: the first request has no `cursor`, and each following request
+  passes back the previous response's `next_cursor` unchanged. Pages are
+  followed until `next_cursor` is `null` or absent. The client sends no
+  `limit`, so the server default page size applies. A failed page rejects the
+  whole call, as does a response without an `items` array.
 - `getItem(transport, id)` → one item; rejects on any non-200 response.
 - `lowStock(items, threshold)` → SKUs with `qty` below the threshold.
 
